{"seq":74,"slug":"distributed-coordination-services","title":"分布式协调服务","stage":"DONE","category":"cs-fundamentals","chapterCount":4,"docCount":12,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/distributed-coordination-services","rating":{"composite":3.66,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.6,"coverage":3.5,"positioning":3.5,"strategic":4},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"分布式协调服务\">分布式协调服务</h1><p>当一个系统从单机扩展到几十、几百个节点，最先崩溃的往往不是计算能力，而是「大家对当前状态的共识」。谁是主节点？这把锁现在归谁？某台机器到底是宕了还是只是网络抖动？这些问题在单机上由操作系统内核一行原子指令就能解决，可一旦跨越网络，它们就变成了分布式系统里最棘手的硬骨头。分布式协调服务正是为了把这些硬骨头集中啃下来而生的一类基础设施——ZooKeeper、etcd、Consul 是它们当中最具代表性的三个。</p>\n<p>这个 hub 用四章把这件事讲透，结构是严格递进的：先打地基，再讲原语，然后看真实系统如何实现这些原语，最后回到工程现场看这些原语怎么被组装成模式、又怎么被用错。</p>\n<p>第一章「基础」回答三个根本问题：协调到底要解决哪些问题（互斥、选主、成员管理），为什么要专门造一个服务而不是在每个应用里各写一套，以及协调服务必须提供什么样的一致性保证才配得上「权威」二字。这一章不碰任何具体产品，只搭概念骨架，是后面所有内容的公理系统。</p>\n<p>第二章「协调原语」把第一章的问题翻译成可调用的接口：分布式锁、领导者选举、租约与监听。这三者是协调服务对外暴露的「系统调用」，几乎所有上层模式都由它们拼装而成。这一章讲清每个原语的正确实现配方，以及它们各自最容易踩的坑（比如锁的 fencing token、选举的惊群效应）。</p>\n<p>第三章「系统」走进三个真实系统的内部：ZooKeeper 的 ZAB 协议、etcd 的 Raft 与 MVCC、Consul 的 gossip 与多数据中心架构。这一章解释「为什么这些系统能提供第二章的原语而且不会骗你」——答案藏在它们各自的共识协议里。</p>\n<p>第四章「模式与实践」收口落地：服务发现、配置协调与屏障，以及一整章的陷阱与反模式。前两节展示原语如何组合成生产级模式，最后一节是用血泪换来的清单——把协调服务当数据库用、watch 风暴、split-brain，都在这里集中解剖。</p>\n<p>读完四章，你应该能在面对「我这个系统需要协调吗、需要哪种、该选谁、怎么用才不出事」时给出有依据的判断，而不是凭感觉抄一段网上的锁代码。</p>\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"foundations","title":"基础","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/distributed-coordination-services/foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"coordination-problems","title":"协调问题：互斥、选主与成员管理","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/distributed-coordination-services/foundations/coordination-problems"},{"seq":2,"slug":"why-coordination-services","title":"为何需要专门的协调服务","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/distributed-coordination-services/foundations/why-coordination-services"},{"seq":3,"slug":"consistency-guarantees","title":"一致性保证","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/distributed-coordination-services/foundations/consistency-guarantees"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"primitives","title":"协调原语","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/distributed-coordination-services/primitives","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"distributed-locks","title":"分布式锁","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/distributed-coordination-services/primitives/distributed-locks"},{"seq":2,"slug":"leader-election","title":"领导者选举","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/distributed-coordination-services/primitives/leader-election"},{"seq":3,"slug":"leases-watches","title":"租约与监听","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/distributed-coordination-services/primitives/leases-watches"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"systems","title":"系统","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/distributed-coordination-services/systems","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"zookeeper-zab","title":"ZooKeeper 与 ZAB 协议","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/distributed-coordination-services/systems/zookeeper-zab"},{"seq":2,"slug":"etcd-raft","title":"etcd 与 Raft","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/distributed-coordination-services/systems/etcd-raft"},{"seq":3,"slug":"consul-others","title":"Consul 与其它协调系统","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/distributed-coordination-services/systems/consul-others"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"patterns","title":"模式与实践","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/distributed-coordination-services/patterns","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"service-discovery","title":"服务发现","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/distributed-coordination-services/patterns/service-discovery"},{"seq":2,"slug":"config-barriers","title":"配置协调与屏障","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/distributed-coordination-services/patterns/config-barriers"},{"seq":3,"slug":"pitfalls-antipatterns","title":"陷阱与反模式","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/distributed-coordination-services/patterns/pitfalls-antipatterns"}]}]}